# Oddrip: tests are mandatory

When you add or change **any** of the following, you **must** add or update tests in the same change — do not mark the task done without them:

- Public methods on `*Service` in `oddrip/*.go` (REST)
- Types with `json` tags in `oddrip/types/*.go`
- WebSocket commands, channels, or message shapes in `oddrip/ws.go` / `oddrip/types/ws.go`

## Required coverage per change

| Change | Test file | Assert |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| New/changed REST method | `oddrip/*_test.go` | HTTP path, method, query params, request body when non-trivial |
| New/changed response/request struct | `oddrip/types/*_test.go` | JSON unmarshal (and marshal if you construct requests) |
| New WS channel or `update_subscription` action | `oddrip/types/ws_test.go` or `oddrip/ws_test.go` | Constant value and/or JSON round-trip |

Use the existing `mockTransport` pattern in `oddrip/client_test.go`.

## Finish checklist

1. Every new public API method has at least one test.
2. Every new/changed exported struct field used in API I/O has a JSON test.
3. Run `go build ./...` and `go test ./...` from repo root — both must pass.
4. Mention new tests in `CHANGELOG.md` when documenting API work.

If you cannot test something (e.g. live WS server behavior), add the closest unit test possible and note the gap — do not skip tests silently.
